# The streaming conformance vectors are byte-exact SSE fixtures: every
# consumer must reproduce their outcomes from the exact bytes on disk, and
# the "allow re-emits input verbatim" contract compares against them
# byte-for-byte. Never let autocrlf rewrite their line endings on checkout.
/tests/conformance/streaming/inputs/*.sse -text

# The differential traces are compared byte for byte against a string the
# Rust exporter builds with LF endings, and are replayed by the .NET SDK from
# the same bytes. Autocrlf rewriting them on checkout makes both fail on
# Windows for a reason that has nothing to do with the behavior under test.
/tests/conformance/streaming/stream-session-traces.txt -text
